\import{fnip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{One equilibrium in the Hopf column}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{In the Hopf column of \ref{fnip-0005}, the steady current is
strictly increasing, so each applied current meets it at one
voltage. The equilibrium is stable when
#{I_{\mathrm{app}}<94} or when #{I_{\mathrm{app}}>212}, and
unstable for the remaining values.
\citet{§3.4.1, p. 56}{ermentrout2010mathematical} states those two
values and calls each change a Hopf bifurcation.}

